    "raw_text": "Multimodal RAG FAQ System — Technical FAQ\nDomain: Retrieval-Augmented Generation, document retrieval, images, and answer generation.\nDataset purpose: This document is a sample knowledge-base source for a Multimodal\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) FAQ system.\nThe visual above is intentionally embedded so the data-extraction module can detect and extract images from the PDF.\nQ1. What is Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)?\nRAG combines retrieval and generation. The system first retrieves relevant information from a knowledge\nbase and then provides that information to a language model to generate an answer.\nQ2. Why does this project use a multimodal RAG approach?\nMany FAQ resources contain both text and visual information such as screenshots, diagrams, and error\nimages. A multimodal system can use both forms of information during retrieval and answer generation.\nQ3. What happens after a user submits a question?\nThe question is encoded for retrieval, relevant knowledge-base content is retrieved and ranked, and the\nselected context is passed to a multimodal language model to generate a response.\nQ4. Why are citations important?\nCitations connect an answer to the source information used to produce it. They allow users and developers\nto verify where the answer came from.\nQ5. What should the system do when the answer is not present in the\nretrieved information?\n\nThe system should avoid inventing an answer and clearly indicate that the available retrieved information\ndoes not contain the required information.\nSource type: Synthetic sample FAQ document | Suitable for local development and extraction testing.",
